    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d134-a6">

                <pb facs="0304" n="208" xml:id="pg208"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 6 in No. 124.]</seg></opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Tsung-li Yamên to Mr.
                            Conger.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1898-12-26"><hi rendition="#italic">December 26,
                        1898</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Your Excellency</hi>: We have the honor to
                    acknowledge the receipt of your excellency’s communications of the 19th and 22d
                    instants, respectively, relative to the missionary conferences to be held at
                    Chungking in January next.</p>
                <p>You therein state that you have wired Rev. Spencer Lewis to postpone said
                    conference and that you have received his reply as follows: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>Too late postpone conference. Parties arriving safely. Others already
                            starting, require Viceroy’s protection.</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>Since the conference can not be postponed, your excellency requests that the
                    viceroy may be ordered to take whatever extra precautions may be necessary to
                    prevent trouble.</p>
                <p>In addition to wiring the viceroy to adopt measures for protection, as in duty
                    bound, we sent this note for your excellency’s consideration.</p>
                <p>Cards of ministers with compliments.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
